{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-80332" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following sets:\n\n$$\nN,\\,Z,\\,Q,\\,R,\\,C\n$$\n\nTo which of these sets does the number $\\pi $ belong?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035971/state.json" "file_sha256" "477ec89755d9a29cde3cf90c26ec1d1502fa5bb92159425b7250d2da55ba7332"} {"question" "q-80332" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035971/assets/67ef97be4b21a74feaae15f3ff30d5077fc1316874df8de79155316a621e4487.png)\n\nRecall the following:\n\n- $N$ represents the set of **natural numbers**.\n\n- $Z$ represents the set of **integers**.\n\n- $Q$ represents the set of **rational numbers**.\n\n- $R$ represents the set of **real numbers**.\n\n- $C$ represents the set of **complex numbers**\n\nWith that in mind, we note the following:\n\n- The number $\\pi $ is not an integer, so it does *not* belong to $Z$ nor to $N,$ so we can write\n\n$$\n\\pi \\notin N,\\,\\pi \\notin Z.\n$$\n\n- Also, notice that $\\pi =3.14159\\,…\\,$ can not be written as the ratio of two integers, so it does *not* belong to $Q$ either, and we can write \n\n$$\n\\pi \\notin Q.\n$$\n\n- Every irrational number is both a real number and a complex number. Consequently, $\\pi $ belongs to both $R$ and $C,$ and we can write\n\n$$\n\\pi \\in R,\\,\\pi \\in C.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$R$ and $C$ only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035971/state.json" "file_sha256" "477ec89755d9a29cde3cf90c26ec1d1502fa5bb92159425b7250d2da55ba7332"} {"question" "q-80332" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035971/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "67ef938e9bb2f2df040845324fbacd55e6190b901c2c4d191d2f829a4d7af248"} {"question" "q-80332" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035971/state.json" "file_sha256" "477ec89755d9a29cde3cf90c26ec1d1502fa5bb92159425b7250d2da55ba7332"} {"question" "q-80332" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$Q,R,$ and $C$ only"] ["text" "$R$ and $C$ only"] ["text" "$R$ only"] ["text" "$Z$ and $Q$ only"] ["text" "$Z,Q,R,$ and $C$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035971/state.json" "file_sha256" "477ec89755d9a29cde3cf90c26ec1d1502fa5bb92159425b7250d2da55ba7332"} {"question" "q-80332" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$R$ and $C$ only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035971/state.json" "file_sha256" "477ec89755d9a29cde3cf90c26ec1d1502fa5bb92159425b7250d2da55ba7332"} {"question" "q-181441" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following sets:\n\n$$\nN,\\,Z,\\,Q,\\,R,\\,C\n$$\n\nTo which of these sets does the number $\\sqrt{-1}$ belong?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035971/state.json" "file_sha256" "477ec89755d9a29cde3cf90c26ec1d1502fa5bb92159425b7250d2da55ba7332"} {"question" "q-181441" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035971/assets/67ef97be4b21a74feaae15f3ff30d5077fc1316874df8de79155316a621e4487.png)\n\nRecall the following:\n\n- $N$ represents the set of **natural numbers**.\n\n- $Z$ represents the set of **integers**.\n\n- $Q$ represents the set of **rational numbers**.\n\n- $R$ represents the set of **real numbers**.\n\n- $C$ represents the set of **complex numbers**\n\nWith that in mind, we note the following:\n\n- First, we note that $\\sqrt{-1}=\\text{i}$ is a complex number. Therefore, we can write\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{-1}\\in C.\n$$\n\n- Since the imaginary part of $\\sqrt{-1}$ is nonzero, it does not belong to $N,Z,Q,$ or $R.$ We can write\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{-1}\\notin N,\\,\\sqrt{-1}\\notin Z,\\,\\sqrt{-1}\\notin Q,\\,\\sqrt{-1}\\notin R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$C$ only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035971/state.json" "file_sha256" "477ec89755d9a29cde3cf90c26ec1d1502fa5bb92159425b7250d2da55ba7332"} {"question" "q-181441" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035971/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "67ef938e9bb2f2df040845324fbacd55e6190b901c2c4d191d2f829a4d7af248"} {"question" "q-181441" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035971/state.json" "file_sha256" "477ec89755d9a29cde3cf90c26ec1d1502fa5bb92159425b7250d2da55ba7332"} {"question" "q-181441" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$C$ only"] ["text" "$N$ and $C$ only"] ["text" "$N,Z,$ and $C$ only"] ["text" "$R$ and $C$ only"] ["text" "$R$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035971/state.json" "file_sha256" "477ec89755d9a29cde3cf90c26ec1d1502fa5bb92159425b7250d2da55ba7332"} {"question" "q-181441" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$C$ only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035971/state.json" "file_sha256" "477ec89755d9a29cde3cf90c26ec1d1502fa5bb92159425b7250d2da55ba7332"} {"question" "q-80234" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following sets:\n\n$$\nN,\\,Z,\\,Q,\\,R,\\,C\n$$\n\nTo which of these sets does the number $-5$ belong?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035971/state.json" "file_sha256" "477ec89755d9a29cde3cf90c26ec1d1502fa5bb92159425b7250d2da55ba7332"} {"question" "q-80234" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035971/assets/67ef97be4b21a74feaae15f3ff30d5077fc1316874df8de79155316a621e4487.png)\n\nRecall the following:\n\n- $N$ represents the set of **natural numbers**.\n\n- $Z$ represents the set of **integers**.\n\n- $Q$ represents the set of **rational numbers**.\n\n- $R$ represents the set of **real numbers**.\n\n- $C$ represents the set of **complex numbers**\n\nWith that in mind, we note the following:\n\n- The number $-5$ is negative, so it does *not* belong to $N,$ and we can write\n\n$$\n-5\\notin N.\n$$\n\n- However, $-5$ is an integer, so it does belong to $Z,$ and we can write\n\n$$\n-5\\in Z.\n$$\n\n- Every integer is a rational, real, and complex number. Consequently, $-5$ belongs to $Q,R,$ and $C,$ and we can write\n\n$$\n-5\\in Q,\\,-5\\in R,\\,-5\\in C.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$Z,Q,R,$ and $C.$\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035971/state.json" "file_sha256" "477ec89755d9a29cde3cf90c26ec1d1502fa5bb92159425b7250d2da55ba7332"} {"question" "q-80234" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035971/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "67ef938e9bb2f2df040845324fbacd55e6190b901c2c4d191d2f829a4d7af248"} {"question" "q-80234" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035971/state.json" "file_sha256" "477ec89755d9a29cde3cf90c26ec1d1502fa5bb92159425b7250d2da55ba7332"} {"question" "q-80234" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$N,Z,Q,R,$ and $C$"] ["text" "$R$ only"] ["text" "$Z$ and $Q$ only"] ["text" "$Z$ only"] ["text" "$Z,Q,R,$ and $C$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035971/state.json" "file_sha256" "477ec89755d9a29cde3cf90c26ec1d1502fa5bb92159425b7250d2da55ba7332"} {"question" "q-80234" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$Z,Q,R,$ and $C$ only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035971/state.json" "file_sha256" "477ec89755d9a29cde3cf90c26ec1d1502fa5bb92159425b7250d2da55ba7332"} {"question" "q-80331" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following sets:\n\n$$\nN,\\,Z,\\,Q,\\,R,\\,C\n$$\n\nTo which of these sets does the number $-\\frac{27}{3}$ belong?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035971/state.json" "file_sha256" "477ec89755d9a29cde3cf90c26ec1d1502fa5bb92159425b7250d2da55ba7332"} {"question" "q-80331" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035971/assets/67ef97be4b21a74feaae15f3ff30d5077fc1316874df8de79155316a621e4487.png)\n\nRecall the following:\n\n- $N$ represents the set of **natural numbers**.\n\n- $Z$ represents the set of **integers**.\n\n- $Q$ represents the set of **rational numbers**.\n\n- $R$ represents the set of **real numbers**.\n\n- $C$ represents the set of **complex numbers**\n\nWith that in mind, we note the following:\n\n- The number $-\\frac{27}{3}=-9$ is negative, so it does *not* belong to $N,$ and we can write\n\n$$\n-\\frac{27}{3}\\notin N.\n$$\n\n- However, $-9$ is an integer, so it does belong to $Z,$ and we can write\n\n$$\n-\\frac{27}{3}\\in Z.\n$$\n\n- Every integer is a rational, real, and complex number. Consequently, $-\\frac{27}{3}$ belongs to $Q,R,$ and $C,$ and we can write\n\n$$\n-\\frac{27}{3}\\in Q,\\,-\\frac{27}{3}\\in R,\\,-\\frac{27}{3}\\in C.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$Z,Q,R,$ and $C$ only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035971/state.json" "file_sha256" "477ec89755d9a29cde3cf90c26ec1d1502fa5bb92159425b7250d2da55ba7332"} {"question" "q-80331" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035971/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "67ef938e9bb2f2df040845324fbacd55e6190b901c2c4d191d2f829a4d7af248"} {"question" "q-80331" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035971/state.json" "file_sha256" "477ec89755d9a29cde3cf90c26ec1d1502fa5bb92159425b7250d2da55ba7332"} {"question" "q-80331" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$C$ only"] ["text" "$N,Z,Q,R,$ and $C$"] ["text" "$Q$ only"] ["text" "$Z$ and $Q$ only"] ["text" "$Z,Q,R,$ and $C$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035971/state.json" "file_sha256" "477ec89755d9a29cde3cf90c26ec1d1502fa5bb92159425b7250d2da55ba7332"} {"question" "q-80331" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$Z,Q,R,$ and $C$ only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035971/state.json" "file_sha256" "477ec89755d9a29cde3cf90c26ec1d1502fa5bb92159425b7250d2da55ba7332"} {"question" "q-181522" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following sets:\n\n$$\nN,\\,Z,\\,Q,\\,R,\\,C\n$$\n\nTo which of these sets does the number $\\sqrt{-4}$ belong?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035971/state.json" "file_sha256" "477ec89755d9a29cde3cf90c26ec1d1502fa5bb92159425b7250d2da55ba7332"} {"question" "q-181522" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035971/assets/67ef97be4b21a74feaae15f3ff30d5077fc1316874df8de79155316a621e4487.png)\n\nRecall the following:\n\n- $N$ represents the set of **natural numbers**.\n\n- $Z$ represents the set of **integers**.\n\n- $Q$ represents the set of **rational numbers**.\n\n- $R$ represents the set of **real numbers**.\n\n- $C$ represents the set of **complex numbers**\n\nWith that in mind, we note the following:\n\n- First, we note that $\\sqrt{-4}=2\\text{i}$ is a complex number. Therefore, we can write\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{-4}\\in C.\n$$\n\n- Since the imaginary part of $\\sqrt{-4}$ is nonzero, it does *not* belong to $N,Z,Q,$ or $R.$ We can write\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{-4}\\notin N,\\,\\sqrt{-4}\\notin Z,\\,\\sqrt{-4}\\notin Q,\\,\\sqrt{-4}\\notin R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$C$ only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035971/state.json" "file_sha256" "477ec89755d9a29cde3cf90c26ec1d1502fa5bb92159425b7250d2da55ba7332"} {"question" "q-181522" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035971/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "67ef938e9bb2f2df040845324fbacd55e6190b901c2c4d191d2f829a4d7af248"} {"question" "q-181522" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035971/state.json" "file_sha256" "477ec89755d9a29cde3cf90c26ec1d1502fa5bb92159425b7250d2da55ba7332"} {"question" "q-181522" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$C$ only"] ["text" "$N,Z,Q$ and $R$ only"] ["text" "$Q$ and $R$ only"] ["text" "$R$ and $C$ only"] ["text" "$R$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035971/state.json" "file_sha256" "477ec89755d9a29cde3cf90c26ec1d1502fa5bb92159425b7250d2da55ba7332"} {"question" "q-181522" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$C$ only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035971/state.json" "file_sha256" "477ec89755d9a29cde3cf90c26ec1d1502fa5bb92159425b7250d2da55ba7332"} {"question" "q-80336" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the numbers below belong to  ${R}_{0}^{-}?$\n\n- $-\\pi $\n- $\\sqrt{3}$\n- $-\\frac{4}{5}$\n- $0$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035971/state.json" "file_sha256" "477ec89755d9a29cde3cf90c26ec1d1502fa5bb92159425b7250d2da55ba7332"} {"question" "q-80336" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Remember that ${R}_{0}^{-}$ is the set of all negative real numbers and $0.$\n\n- $-\\pi $ belongs to ${R}_{0}^{-}.\\,✓$\n\n- $\\sqrt{3}$ is a positive number, so it does *not* belong to ${R}_{0}^{-}.\\,\\times $\n\n- $-\\frac{4}{5}$ belongs to ${R}_{0}^{-}.\\,✓$\n\n- $0$ belongs to ${R}_{0}^{-}.\\,✓$\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"I, III, and IV only\"." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035971/state.json" "file_sha256" "477ec89755d9a29cde3cf90c26ec1d1502fa5bb92159425b7250d2da55ba7332"} {"question" "q-80336" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/1